# Testing & Development Workflow Rules

## �� Testing Patterns

### Component Testing

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Component test structure
import { render, screen, fireEvent } from "@testing-library/react";
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from "@tanstack/react-query";
import Component from "./Component";

const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: {
    queries: { retry: false },
  },
});

function renderWithProviders(component: React.ReactElement) {
  return render(
    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>{component}</QueryClientProvider>
  );
}

describe("Component", () => {
  it("should render correctly", () => {
    renderWithProviders(<Component />);
    expect(screen.getByText("Expected Text")).toBeInTheDocument();
  });

  it("should handle user interactions", () => {
    renderWithProviders(<Component />);
    const button = screen.getByRole("button");
    fireEvent.click(button);
    expect(screen.getByText("Clicked")).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

### MUST FOLLOW Rules

✅ **ALWAYS** write tests for all components
✅ **ALWAYS** test user interactions and edge cases
✅ **ALWAYS** use proper testing utilities (React Testing Library)
✅ **ALWAYS** mock external dependencies
✅ **ALWAYS** test error states and loading states
✅ **ALWAYS** maintain good test coverage
✅ **ALWAYS** use descriptive test names

### NEVER DO Rules

❌ **NEVER** test implementation details
❌ **NEVER** forget to test error scenarios
❌ **NEVER** write tests that are too brittle
❌ **NEVER** forget to clean up after tests
❌ **NEVER** test multiple things in one test
❌ **NEVER** forget to test accessibility

### Development Workflow

```bash
# ✅ CORRECT - Development workflow
# 1. Create feature branch
git checkout -b feature/new-component

# 2. Write tests first (TDD)
npm test -- --watch

# 3. Implement feature
# Write component code

# 4. Run linting and formatting
npm run lint
npm run format

# 5. Run all tests
npm test

# 6. Build and check for errors
npm run build

# 7. Commit with proper message
git commit -m "feat: add new component with tests"

# 8. Push and create PR
git push origin feature/new-component
```

### Debugging Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT - Debugging with proper logging
const DEBUG = process.env.NODE_ENV === "development";

function debugLog(message: string, data?: any) {
  if (DEBUG) {
    console.log(`[DEBUG] ${message}`, data);
  }
}

function Component() {
  useEffect(() => {
    debugLog("Component mounted");
    return () => debugLog("Component unmounted");
  }, []);

  const handleClick = () => {
    debugLog("Button clicked");
    // Handle click
  };

  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Click me</button>;
}
```

